                <pb facs="0481" n="401" xml:id="pg401"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">863.51 Relief Credits/233: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Ives</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-05-22T16:00:00+01:00">May 22, 1930—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 22—2:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>26. Department’s 25, May 19, 5 p.m. Danish note May 14 mentioned only customs and
                    tobacco revenues.</p>
                <p>In a further note, dated May 20, Foreign Office states that by declaration of
                    Leith-Ross, dated April 16, last, Denmark has renounced its liens on the
                    revenues of the Austrian Government derived from the customs and tobacco
                    monopoly as well as such of the other revenues as may from time to time be
                    required as guarantee in favor of the creditors of the new loan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ives</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
